A very ordinary early game.  I did find a magic lamp, but the minetown
temple was cross-aligned.  I never get to minetown at low level, so the
effort yielded only a few points of protection.  I was looking forward
only to a hard slog and an early death - the pattern of this Arc's
predecessors.  But on Dlvl 10, I found a statue of a Valk named Scient
and she had the most wonderful stash - including rotted speed boots, a
cloak of displacement, a ring of levitation and a spellbook of
identify.  Even better, there was a Lawful altar close by.  I soon had
GSDM, was invisible and displaced, had a full pack ID and had geno'd L
and ;.

I sac'ed for Grayswandir, but the Q-man gave me garbage artifact after
garbage artifact.  Woohoo, Ogresmasher.  So I decided to head for the
castle, went around back, wished up Grayswandir, a HoB and a magic
marker and got my AC to -34.  Gehennom sucked without magic mapping
(I've ascended a wizard before), I should've wished for the spellbook.
Nothing gave me any trouble dual wielding Grayswandir and a silver
saber - including minotaurs, the only monster that ever took my HP
below 90% of max.

After finding the VS, I did prep by digging out Gehennom and
fooproofing everything.  I quaffed all my b!oFH, so I only had one that
I found on the run up when I got to the planes.  I had three wands of
death and used them liberally on the high priest and then Rodney on the
way up.  The mysterious force was annoying, but not overly so.  Rodney
only double troubled me once.  I recharged my wands of death before
exiting the dungeon.

No trouble on the planes, used a wand of teleport whenever anything
nasty got near me.  Invisible, displaced, stealthy and very fast did me
well to the end.  I teleported and dodged everyone except Pestilence
who got the wand of death.  Wrong altar first time - didn't have to go
all the way in because I had conflict on and saw the high priest
getting attacked by a vampire - right altar second choice.  Didn't
hesitate to #offer the amulet, and ...

